      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of perceived judgment from others sounds incredibly isolating and painful right now. It is understandable that you feel the foundation of your past self is gone, and that this feels like a punishment. Instead of focusing on 'rebuilding' all at once, sometimes the first step is simply allowing yourself to acknowledge the depth of this grief without judgment. Please consider reaching out to a crisis line or mental health professional who can offer immediate, non-judgmental support during this intense time.",
      "source": "target",
